### Crypto Tracker API — manual requests (Stage 0: base setup, Stage 2: api-rest,
### Stage 3: auth-firebase, Stage 4: watchlists, Stage 5: alertas-email)
### Use with the REST Client extension (VS Code) or any compatible .http runner.
### Run `npm run dev` first, then send requests against http://localhost:3000.
### Stage 2 requires a seeded catalog (`npm run seed:coins`) and at least one
### `poll-prices` run (`npm run job:poll-prices` or `npm run dev:worker`) for
### non-empty responses.
### Stage 3 requests need a Firebase ID token: get one with
### `npm run auth:create-test-user -- --email ... --password ...` followed by
### `npm run --silent auth:token -- --email ... --password ...` (see the
### README's "Firebase Auth: development scripts and the Auth emulator"
### section), then replace `<your-id-token>` below with it. The admin requests
### additionally need that user promoted with
### `npm run user:set-role -- --email ... --role admin` (or created with
### `auth:create-test-user --admin` directly). `ADMIN_API_KEY`/`X-Admin-Key`
### no longer exist.
### Stage 5 requests additionally need: MongoDB running as a replica set and a
### local Mailpit instance (`docker compose up` — see the README's "Getting
### started"), and the worker's `SMTP_HOST`/`SMTP_PORT`/`SMTP_USER`/
### `SMTP_PASS`/`MAIL_FROM` environment variables set (e.g. `SMTP_HOST=localhost`,
### `SMTP_PORT=1025`, `MAIL_FROM=alerts@crypto-tracker.local` for local Mailpit
### — see the README's "Environment variables" table for every variable's
### exact default). The caller's Firebase account additionally needs a
### **verified** email to create an alert (`EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED` otherwise).
### View everything the worker actually sends at http://localhost:8025.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@idToken = <your-id-token>
@adminIdToken = <your-admin-id-token>

### Liveness: never touches the database.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Readiness: checks Mongo connectivity (200 when up, 503 when down).
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Request id is echoed back when supplied by the client.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
X-Request-Id: manual-test-123

### Unknown route -> 404 NOT_FOUND with the global error format.
GET {{baseUrl}}/no-existe

### Malformed JSON body -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR ("JSON inválido").
POST {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

{"invalid": json}

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): coin read endpoints
### ============================================================

### List coins: default page/limit, sorted by market cap descending.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins

### List coins with explicit pagination, sort and order.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins?page=1&limit=10&sort=change24h&order=asc

### List coins matching a name/symbol prefix (case-insensitive).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins?q=bit

### Unknown query param -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (E2-4).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins?foo=1

### Coin detail.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin

### Unknown coin -> 404 NOT_FOUND.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/no-existe

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): price history
### ============================================================

### Raw points over a short window (interval auto-selected as "raw").
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?from=2026-09-22T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-22T06:00:00Z

### Explicit interval=raw.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=raw&from=2026-09-22T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-22T06:00:00Z

### Bucketed OHLC candles (interval=1h) over 7 days, with a 3-bucket SMA.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=1h&from=2026-09-16T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z&sma=3

### Bucketed OHLC candles (interval=1d) over 90 days.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=1d&from=2026-06-25T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z

### raw over a range exceeding the 7-day cap -> 400 suggesting interval=1h (E2-8).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=raw&from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): price stats
### ============================================================

### Default range (24h).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/stats

### 7-day range.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/stats?range=7d

### 90-day range (the range RNF-2.1 sets a p95 < 200ms budget for).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/stats?range=90d

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): status
### ============================================================

### Public worker-health summary — no admin key required.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/status

### ============================================================
### Stage 3 (auth-firebase): the authenticated user's own profile
### ============================================================

### Without a token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED (E3-1).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me

### With a valid token: provisions the profile on first call, then returns it.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Update the editable field.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"displayName": "Nico"}

### `role`/`email` are not editable -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (E3-8).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"role": "admin"}

### Deletes this application's own profile only (204); the Firebase account
### survives and re-provisions an empty profile on the next authenticated call.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### ============================================================
### Stage 2/3: admin job-runs (requireAuth + requireRole('admin'))
### ============================================================

### Without a token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED (E3-10; the old X-Admin-Key header,
### if sent instead, is simply ignored and still yields 401).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs

### Authenticated but not an admin -> 403 FORBIDDEN (E3-9).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Paginated list, filtered by status, with an admin token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs?status=success,partial&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Filtered by jobName and a startedAt range.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs?jobName=poll-prices&from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Job run detail by id (replace with a real _id from the list above).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b456
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Malformed id -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs/not-an-object-id
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### ============================================================
### Stage 4 (watchlists): the authenticated user's own watchlist
### ============================================================

### Without a token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist

### List the caller's watchlist (default sort: addedAt desc).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Sorted by 24h change, descending (E4-13).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist?sort=change24h&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Unknown query param -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (no pagination params accepted here).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist?page=1
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Add a coin (201 + Location header). Requires bitcoin to exist and be active
### (seeded by default — see "Getting started" / seed:coins).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin", "note": "largo plazo"}

### Adding the same coin again -> 409 CONFLICT (E4-2).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin"}

### An unknown or inactive coingeckoId -> 404 NOT_FOUND (E4-3).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "no-existe"}

### A client-supplied userId is rejected as an unknown field -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (RF-4.5).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin", "userId": "000000000000000000000000"}

### Update the note (mixed-case path id is normalized to lowercase first).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist/Bitcoin
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"note": "actualizado"}

### Patching a coin not followed -> 404 NOT_FOUND (E4-7).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist/ethereum
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"note": "no la sigo"}

### Remove a coin — always 204, even if it was never followed (E4-6).
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist/bitcoin
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### A malformed coingeckoId -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/watchlist/Not_Valid!
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### ============================================================
### Stage 4 (watchlists): admin coin management (requireAuth + requireRole('admin'))
### ============================================================

### Authenticated but not an admin -> 403 FORBIDDEN (E4-9).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin"}

### Paginated list, including inactive coins, each with watchersCount.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Filtered to only inactive coins.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins?isActive=false
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Add a new coin — validated against CoinGecko first (consumes one API call).
### 201 if it's new, 200 if it existed inactive (reactivated), 409 if already active.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "chainlink"}

### An id CoinGecko doesn't recognize -> 422 UNPROCESSABLE / UNKNOWN_COINGECKO_ID (E4-10).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "not-a-real-coingecko-id"}

### Deactivate a coin — 200 with the coin and its watchersCount, so the admin
### sees the blast radius before/after (E4-8).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins/bitcoin
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"isActive": false}

### Reactivate it.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins/bitcoin
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"isActive": true}

### No DELETE endpoint exists for coins (falls through to the global 404 —
### deleting would orphan watchlist references and price history).
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/coins/bitcoin
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### ============================================================
### Stage 5 (alertas-email): the authenticated user's own alerts
### ============================================================

### Without a token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts

### List the caller's alerts (default: all statuses, createdAt desc).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Filtered by status (comma-separated) and coin.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts?status=armed,triggered&coingeckoId=bitcoin
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Create a PRICE_BELOW alert. Requires bitcoin to exist and be active, and
### the caller's email to be verified. 201 + Location header; meta reports
### the coin's current value and whether the condition is already met.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin", "type": "PRICE_BELOW", "threshold": 70000, "note": "largo plazo"}

### Create a CHANGE_24H_ABS_GTE alert with its own threshold range (0.1-100).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin", "type": "CHANGE_24H_ABS_GTE", "threshold": 5, "cooldownMinutes": 30}

### A threshold outside its type's range -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin", "type": "CHANGE_24H_ABS_GTE", "threshold": 150}

### A caller whose email isn't verified -> 422 UNPROCESSABLE / EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED (E5-1).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "bitcoin", "type": "PRICE_ABOVE", "threshold": 80000}

### An unknown or inactive coingeckoId -> 404 NOT_FOUND.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "no-existe", "type": "PRICE_ABOVE", "threshold": 80000}

### Already at ALERTS_MAX_ACTIVE armed/triggered alerts -> 422 UNPROCESSABLE / LIMIT_REACHED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"coingeckoId": "ethereum", "type": "PRICE_ABOVE", "threshold": 5000}

### Alert detail by id (replace with a real _id from a listing above).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b789
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Malformed id -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/not-an-object-id
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Another user's alert is reported as 404, never 403 (E5-16).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b000
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### PATCH: disable an alert (status -> disabled, whatever it was before).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b789
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"enabled": false}

### PATCH: re-enable a disabled alert (status -> armed; 422 LIMIT_REACHED if
### the caller is already at ALERTS_MAX_ACTIVE).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b789
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"enabled": true}

### PATCH: change the threshold. If the alert was `triggered`, this re-arms
### it (status -> armed) without resetting lastTriggeredAt/triggerCount.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b789
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"threshold": 65000}

### `type` is immutable -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (the field isn't even part of
### the PATCH schema, so it's rejected the same way an unknown field is).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b789
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "PRICE_ABOVE"}

### Delete an alert. Always 204; any of its `pending` notifications move to
### `cancelled`.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/alerts/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b789
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### ============================================================
### Stage 5 (alertas-email): the authenticated user's own notifications
### ============================================================

### List the caller's notification history (masked `to`, only `lastError.code`).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Filtered to failed notifications only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/notifications?status=failed
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### ============================================================
### Stage 5 (alertas-email): admin notifications (requireAuth + requireRole('admin'))
### ============================================================

### Authenticated but not an admin -> 403 FORBIDDEN.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Paginated list with full diagnostic detail (complete lastError, lockedBy).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Filtered by status and a createdAt range.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?status=failed&from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Retry a `failed` notification -> 200, status becomes `pending` with
### attempts: 0 and a cleared lastError (E5-17). Replace with a real _id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b900/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Retrying a notification that isn't `failed` (e.g. already `sent`) -> 409
### CONFLICT, unchanged (E5-17). An unknown id -> 404 NOT_FOUND instead.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b901/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Send an immediate test email to the calling admin's own address, bypassing
### the outbox entirely (no `notifications` document is created). 200 with a
### `messageId`; 502 UPSTREAM_ERROR with the mailer's error code if SMTP is
### unavailable. Check http://localhost:8025 for the result.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/test-email
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
